CMS explicitly describes the 21-day refund figure as an average based on operational data, so that claim is supported. I found a separate arithmetic problem: a 60% gross-price drop against a 45% prior rebate implies roughly a 27% net reduction under comparable assumptions, not single digits to low teens.
